This notebook walks through the core nano-graphrag workflow: load text, build a knowledge graph, query it with different modes, then dive deep into the resulting graph structure with rich visualization and analysis.

::: {#setup .cell cache='true' execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import json
import logging
import time
from collections import Counter
from pathlib import Path

logging.basicConfig(level=logging.WARNING)
logging.getLogger("nano-graphrag").setLevel(logging.WARNING)

WORKING_DIR = Path("./_cache/01_quick_start")
WORKING_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
```
:::


::: {#imports .cell cache='true' execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
from nano_graphrag import GraphRAG, QueryParam
```
:::


## Load Sample Text

We use the first 400 lines of *A Christmas Carol* from the test fixtures.

::: {#load-text .cell cache='true' execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
with open("../tests/fixtures/mock_data.txt", encoding="utf-8-sig") as f:
    lines = f.readlines()

text = "".join(lines[:400])
print(f"Loaded {len(text):,} characters ({len(text.splitlines())} lines)")
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}
```
Loaded 15,650 characters (400 lines)
```
:::
:::


## Initialize GraphRAG

API credentials come from environment variables (managed via dotenvx).

::: {#init-rag .cell cache='true' execution_count=4}
``` {.python .cell-code}
rag = GraphRAG(
    working_dir=str(WORKING_DIR),
    enable_llm_cache=True,
)
print(f"LLM model:      {rag.llm_model}")
print(f"Embedding model: {rag.embedding_model}")
```

